# Full guides only — no shortened versions

When the user pastes a pillar / how-to guide draft (or asks to publish one from chat / `_user-drafts`):

## Do

- Keep the **full body** one-to-one: all parts, tables, checklists, budgets, addresses, error lists.
- Add Emigro **frontmatter**, official_sources, CTA, covers / review-tiers, and cross-links.
- Soften only what fact-check requires (wrong thresholds, outdated law, absolute street addresses if unverified) — as short overlays or footnotes, **not** by cutting sections.
- Prefer the user's structure and wording over a condensed Emigro rewrite.

## Do not

- Create “практическая выжимка”, abbreviated Parts, or “ориентир-таблицы вместо полного текста”.
- Drop sections to “match” shorter guides or reduce token/file size.
- Replace a full draft with a summary and call it published.

## If unsure

Ship the full paste with frontmatter first; fact-check patches second. Never shorten first.
